    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "fece31d8",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Diaphragm and Shear Wall Design"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "cb305da4",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Redundancy Factor\n",
        "\n",
        "The redundancy factor, $\\rho$, is either 1.3 or 1.0 according to ASCE 7-16 12.3.4. \\\n",
        "\n",
        "No single story resists more than 35% of the shear force (see $C_{vx}$ in \\autoref{tab:seismic_forces_calculation_table}), so all values of $\\rho$ are $1.0$.\n",
        "\n",
        "Table: Redundancy Factors {#tab:redundancy_factors}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "940c568f",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Envelope Procedure\n",
        "\n",
        "We will envelope the forces with a fully flexible diaphragm assumption and a fully rigid diaphragm assumption."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "e462f7a6",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Flexible Diaphragm Assumption\n",
        "\n",
        "We will uniformly distribute the shear forces across the diaphragms based on tributary areas of each level. This removes some nuance in the distribution of floor weight distribution (corridors are 17% heavier than the rest of the floors, for instance), but the vast majority of the area of each level is typical floor weight (30 psf) instead of corridor weight (35 psf)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "c90aca48",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "$$\n",
        "f_{p,x} = F_x / A_{level}\n",
        "$$"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 40,
      "id": "81d6654f",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [
        {
          "data": {
            "text/latex": [
              "\\begin{equation*}\n",
              "\\begin{aligned}\n",
              "A_{level} &= 1.541e+04\\ \\mathrm{ft}^{2} \\; \n",
              "\\\\\n",
              "f_{p,roof} &= 4.627\\ \\mathrm{psf} \\; \n",
              "\\\\\n",
              "f_{p,4} &= 4.558\\ \\mathrm{psf} \\; \n",
              "\\\\\n",
              "f_{p,3} &= 3.096\\ \\mathrm{psf} \\; \n",
              "\\\\\n",
              "f_{p,2} &= 1.629\\ \\mathrm{psf} \\; \n",
              "\\end{aligned}\n",
              "\\end{equation*}"
            ],
            "text/plain": [
              "<IPython.core.display.Latex object>"
            ]
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "output_type": "display_data"
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "%%render\n",
        "A_level\n",
        "f_p__roof = seismic_loads.loc[\"Roof\", \"F_x\"] * 1000 * lb / A_level\n",
        "f_p__4 = seismic_loads.loc[\"Level 4\", \"F_x\"] * 1000 * lb / A_level\n",
        "f_p__3 = seismic_loads.loc[\"Level 3\", \"F_x\"] * 1000 * lb / A_level\n",
        "f_p__2 = seismic_loads.loc[\"Level 2\", \"F_x\"] * 1000 * lb / A_level"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "2491f399",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#### North-South Direction"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "a48f8571",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Most of the shear walls are not in line which presents an issue: if we assume a diaphragm is the full depth, there will be an extremely long collector element without a shear wall on both sides. We will avoid this by just assuming the flexible diaphragm does not extend the full depth and instead is just tributary to the nearest wall (\\autoref{fig:diaphragm_trib_area}). This means that there are essentially two diaphragms through the depth of the building. This is a rough approximation to ensure all the shear load is resolved in the shear walls. \\\n",
        "\n",
        "The walls that are close to inline (A-5 and A-5.1, A-6 and A-6.1, and A-9 and A-9.1) in reality will be treated as inline and have collectors to transfer the shear load from the diaphragm to those walls.\n",
        "\n",
        "Proper detailing will be done to ensure continuity through the depth of the diaphragm.\n",
        "\n",
        "![Shear walls (thick red lines) in plan view with their (colored) tributary areas.](images/shear_wall_tributary_area.png){width=60% #fig:diaphragm_trib_area}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 41,
      "id": "986a7add",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Plan dimensions\n",
        "l_A1__A2 = (31 + 11 / 12) * ft\n",
        "l_A2__A3 = (17 + 11 / 12) * ft\n",
        "l_A3__A4 = (26 + 4 / 12) * ft\n",
        "l_A4__A5 = (21 + 4 / 12) * ft\n",
        "l_A5__A6 = (24 + 8 / 12) * ft\n",
        "l_A6__A7 = (34 + 4 / 12) * ft\n",
        "l_A7__A8 = (26 + 1 / 12) * ft\n",
        "l_A8__A9 = (21 + 4 / 12) * ft\n",
        "l_A9__A10 = (31 + 1 / 12) * ft\n",
        "\n",
        "l_A1__A24 = (40 + 1 / 12) * ft\n",
        "l_A24__A35 = (23 + 8 / 12) * ft\n",
        "l_A35__A51 = (34 + 4 / 12) * ft\n",
        "l_A51__A61 = (24 + 8 / 12) * ft\n",
        "l_A61__A68 = (24 + 8 / 12) * ft\n",
        "l_A68__A82 = (38 + 3 / 12) * ft\n",
        "l_A82__A89 = (17 + 11 / 12) * ft\n",
        "l_A89__A10 = (31 + 5 / 12) * ft\n",
        "\n",
        "l_A37__A4 = (8 + 10 / 12) * ft\n",
        "l_A3__A37 = l_A3__A4 - l_A37__A4\n",
        "l_A78__A82 = (8 + 10 / 12) * ft\n",
        "l_A68__A78 = l_A68__A82 - l_A78__A82\n",
        "\n",
        "d_trib = 67 / 2 * ft"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 42,
      "id": "0e712d4b",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Wall tributary widths\n",
        "t_w__A2 = l_A1__A2 + (l_A2__A3 + l_A3__A37) / 2\n",
        "t_w__A24 = (l_A1__A24 - L_jog) + ((l_A24__A35 + l_A35__A51) / 2)\n",
        "t_w__A37 = ((l_A2__A3 + l_A3__A37) / 2) + (l_A37__A4 / 2)\n",
        "t_w__A4 = (l_A37__A4 / 2) + (l_A4__A5 / 2)\n",
        "t_w__A5 = (l_A4__A5 / 2) + (l_A5__A6 / 2)\n",
        "t_w__A51 = ((l_A24__A35 + l_A35__A51) / 2) + (l_A51__A61 / 2)\n",
        "t_w__A6 = (l_A5__A6 / 2) + (l_A6__A7 / 2)\n",
        "t_w__A61 = (l_A51__A61 / 2) + (l_A61__A68 / 2)\n",
        "t_w__A68 = (l_A61__A68 / 2) + (l_A68__A78 / 2)\n",
        "t_w__A7 = (l_A6__A7 / 2) + (l_A7__A8 / 2)\n",
        "t_w__A78 = (l_A68__A78 / 2) + (l_A78__A82 / 2)\n",
        "t_w__A8 = (l_A7__A8 / 2) + (l_A8__A9 / 2)\n",
        "t_w__A82 = (l_A78__A82 / 2) + (l_A82__A89 / 2)\n",
        "t_w__A89 = (l_A82__A89 / 2) + l_A89__A10\n",
        "t_w__A9 = (l_A8__A9 / 2) + (l_A9__A10 - L_jog)\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "96e563a5",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Shear wall shear forces are tabulated in \\autoref{tab:shear_wall_forces_roof_ns}, \\autoref{tab:shear_wall_forces_level4_ns}, \\autoref{tab:shear_wall_forces_level3_ns}, and \\autoref{tab:shear_wall_forces_level2_ns}. \\\n",
        "\n",
        "Note that the cumulative shear force, $F_{x,cum}$, is cumulative from the Roof downwards. For example, Level 3 includes the shear forces from the Roof, Level 4, and Level 3."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 43,
      "id": "ae2370f8",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "levels = [\"Roof\", \"Level 4\", \"Level 3\", \"Level 2\"]\n",
        "walls = [\n",
        "    \"A-2\",\n",
        "    \"A-2.4\",\n",
        "    \"A-3.7\",\n",
        "    \"A-4\",\n",
        "    \"A-5\",\n",
        "    \"A-5.1\",\n",
        "    \"A-6\",\n",
        "    \"A-6.1\",\n",
        "    \"A-6.8\",\n",
        "    \"A-7\",\n",
        "    \"A-7.8\",\n",
        "    \"A-8\",\n",
        "    \"A-8.2\",\n",
        "    \"A-8.9\",\n",
        "    \"A-9\",\n",
        "]\n",
        "\n",
        "index = pd.MultiIndex.from_product([levels, walls], names=[\"Level\", \"Wall\"])\n",
        "\n",
        "diaphragm_flexible_ns = pd.DataFrame(index=index)\n",
        "diaphragm_flexible_ns.loc[\"Roof\", \"tributary weight\"] = float(f_p__roof)\n",
        "diaphragm_flexible_ns.loc[\"Level 4\", \"tributary weight\"] = float(f_p__4)\n",
        "diaphragm_flexible_ns.loc[\"Level 3\", \"tributary weight\"] = float(f_p__3)\n",
        "diaphragm_flexible_ns.loc[\"Level 2\", \"tributary weight\"] = float(f_p__2)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Add wall tributary lengths to df\n",
        "wall_trib_widths = {\n",
        "    \"A-2\": float(t_w__A2),\n",
        "    \"A-2.4\": float(t_w__A24),\n",
        "    \"A-3.7\": float(t_w__A37),\n",
        "    \"A-4\": float(t_w__A4),\n",
        "    \"A-5\": float(t_w__A5),\n",
        "    \"A-5.1\": float(t_w__A51),\n",
        "    \"A-6\": float(t_w__A6),\n",
        "    \"A-6.1\": float(t_w__A61),\n",
        "    \"A-6.8\": float(t_w__A68),\n",
        "    \"A-7\": float(t_w__A7),\n",
        "    \"A-7.8\": float(t_w__A78),\n",
        "    \"A-8\": float(t_w__A8),\n",
        "    \"A-8.2\": float(t_w__A82),\n",
        "    \"A-8.9\": float(t_w__A89),\n",
        "    \"A-9\": float(t_w__A9),\n",
        "}\n",
        "diaphragm_flexible_ns[\"tributary width\"] = diaphragm_flexible_ns.index.get_level_values(\n",
        "    \"Wall\"\n",
        ").map(wall_trib_widths)\n",
        "diaphragm_flexible_ns[\"tributary depth\"] = float(d_trib)\n",
        "diaphragm_flexible_ns[\"tributary area\"] = (\n",
        "    diaphragm_flexible_ns[\"tributary depth\"] * diaphragm_flexible_ns[\"tributary width\"]\n",
        ")\n",
        "level_area = diaphragm_flexible_ns[\"tributary area\"].sum() / 4\n",
        "\n",
        "# Ensure that the calculated areas from earlier and tributary areas match\n",
        "assert np.isclose(level_area, float(A_level)), (\n",
        "    \"Shear wall tributary areas and level area do not match up. Ensure you are including all areas in your calculations\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "diaphragm_flexible_ns[\"floor shear\"] = (\n",
        "    diaphragm_flexible_ns[\"tributary area\"] * diaphragm_flexible_ns[\"tributary weight\"]\n",
        ")\n",
        "diaphragm_flexible_ns[\"cumulative shear\"] = diaphragm_flexible_ns.groupby(level=\"Wall\")[\n",
        "    \"floor shear\"\n",
        "].cumsum()\n",
        "\n",
        "l_aa__ab = 30 + 9 / 12\n",
        "l_ac__ad = 30 + 9 / 12\n",
        "l_stairwall = 20\n",
        "wall_lengths = {\n",
        "    \"A-2\": l_aa__ab,\n",
        "    \"A-2.4\": l_ac__ad,\n",
        "    \"A-3.7\": l_stairwall,\n",
        "    \"A-4\": l_stairwall,\n",
        "    \"A-5\": l_aa__ab,\n",
        "    \"A-5.1\": l_ac__ad,\n",
        "    \"A-6\": l_aa__ab,\n",
        "    \"A-6.1\": l_ac__ad,\n",
        "    \"A-6.8\": l_ac__ad,\n",
        "    \"A-7\": l_aa__ab,\n",
        "    \"A-7.8\": l_stairwall,\n",
        "    \"A-8\": l_aa__ab,\n",
        "    \"A-8.2\": l_stairwall,\n",
        "    \"A-8.9\": l_ac__ad,\n",
        "    \"A-9\": l_aa__ab,\n",
        "}\n",
        "diaphragm_flexible_ns[\"wall length\"] = diaphragm_flexible_ns.index.get_level_values(\n",
        "    \"Wall\"\n",
        ").map(wall_lengths)\n",
        "diaphragm_flexible_ns[\"unit shear\"] = (\n",
        "    diaphragm_flexible_ns[\"cumulative shear\"] / diaphragm_flexible_ns[\"wall length\"]\n",
        ")\n",
        "load_factor = 0.7\n",
        "diaphragm_flexible_ns[\"factored unit shear\"] = (\n",
        "    diaphragm_flexible_ns[\"unit shear\"] * load_factor\n",
        ")\n",
        "diaphragm_flexible_ns[\"sheathed sides\"] = 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 44,
      "id": "34639935",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Rename columns for display with LaTeX formatting for units and subscripts/superscripts\n",
        "df_display = diaphragm_flexible_ns[\n",
        "    diaphragm_flexible_ns.columns.difference(\n",
        "        [\"tributary width\", \"tributary depth\"], sort=False\n",
        "    )\n",
        "].copy()\n",
        "column_name_map = {\n",
        "    \"tributary weight\": \"$w_{trib}$ [psf]\",\n",
        "    # \"tributary width\": \"$l_{trib}$ [ft]\",\n",
        "    # \"tributary depth\": \"$d_{trib}$ [ft]\",\n",
        "    \"tributary area\": \"$A$ [ft$^2$]\",\n",
        "    \"floor shear\": \"$F_x$ [lbf]\",\n",
        "    \"cumulative shear\": \"$F_{x,cum}$ [lbf]\",\n",
        "    \"wall length\": \"$l_{wall}$ [ft]\",\n",
        "    \"unit shear\": \"$v$ [plf]\",\n",
        "    \"factored unit shear\": \"$0.7 v$ [lbf]\",\n",
        "}\n",
        "df_display.rename(columns=column_name_map, errors=\"raise\", inplace=True)"
      ]
    },
